    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nFirst thank you for your hard work on mini. I started to use it 8 months ago for replacement of surround and from time to time I like to check your other modules ; pairs, cursorword and starter are now in my toolbox and probably others in the future :)\r\n\r\nTo get back on this bug, this is probably a very edge/unsual case but since it crashes nvim I prefer to report!\r\n\r\nSome terminals like [kitty](https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/conf/#opt-kitty.window_padding_width) or [wezterm](https://wezfurlong.org/wezterm/config/lua/config/window_padding.html?highlight=padding#window_padding) allow to set a padding that can be modified at runtime with user defined keybinds. I usually reset my default padding to 0 when I'm working with nvim to get the maximum space.\r\n\r\nI notice whenever `mini.starter` is displayed and focused if I reset this padding, nvim crashes, arguing:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndouble free or corruption (!prev)\r\nzsh: segmentation fault (core dumped)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI tested on zsh and bash, with kitty and wezterm, same behaviour.\r\n\r\nThis is not happening if I do this operation on other buffers, even if starter is displayed.\r\nMy workaround for now is to remove `MiniStarterBuffer` augroup when hooked on `MiniStarterOpened`\r\nSo, I might be wrong but I suspect `Mini.refresh()` to be the culprit. \r\n\r\nLast (and weird) thing, this is not happening if I had more padding (!?) \n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.9.0-dev-128-gef4c339fb\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\r\n$ kitty -o allow_remote_control=yes -o window_padding_width=20 -o map=\"alt+0 remote_control set-spacing padding=0\" nvim -nu minimal.lua\r\n```\r\n\r\nContent of minimal.lua\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.cmd([[set runtimepath=$VIMRUNTIME]])\r\nvim.cmd([[set packpath=/tmp/nvim/site]])\r\n\r\nlocal package_root = '/tmp/nvim/site/pack'\r\nlocal packer_install_path = package_root .. '/packer/start/packer.nvim'\r\n\r\nlocal function load_plugins()\r\n    require('packer').startup({\r\n        {\r\n            'wbthomason/packer.nvim',\r\n            'echasnovski/mini.nvim',\r\n        },\r\n        config = {\r\n            package_root = package_root,\r\n            compile_path = packer_install_path .. '/plugin/packer_compiled.lua',\r\n            display = { non_interactive = true },\r\n        },\r\n    })\r\nend\r\n\r\n_G.load_config = function()\r\n    require('mini.starter').setup()\r\n    require('mini.starter').open()\r\nend\r\n\r\nif vim.fn.isdirectory(packer_install_path) == 0 then\r\n    print('Installing plugins and dependencies...')\r\n    vim.fn.system({ 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/wbthomason/packer.nvim', packer_install_path })\r\nend\r\n\r\nload_plugins()\r\nrequire('packer').sync()\r\nvim.cmd( [[autocmd User PackerComplete ++once echo \"Ready!\" | lua load_config()]])\r\n```\r\n\r\nWait for mini.starter to display. Then hit `alt+0` to reset padding.\r\n\r\nIf you invert the values it works:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n$ kitty -o allow_remote_control=yes -o window_padding_width=0 -o map=\"alt+0 remote_control set-spacing padding=20\" nvim -nu minimal.lua\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nnvim should not crash\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nnvim crashes",
