        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Not related but since we're talking about `MiniStarter.refresh` I notice refreshing from another buffer like a treeview or help pane, `:lua MiniStarter.refresh(buf_mini_starter_id)` won't correctly align, if I issue the exact same command when it is focused, this works. am I missing something?\r\n\r\nNo, you don't miss anything. This is a bug because aligning hook currently [gets width from current window](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a57bd4bc25bedd8c0c7d27899f86fa909d157752/lua/mini/starter.lua#L716). This is a part I overlooked when implementing #82 - previously it was only single Starter buffer allowed.\r\n\r\nI'll fix it. Thanks again for noticing!",
